and Burma Border Consortium</publisher-name><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>60</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hung le</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Vries</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Giao</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name><name><surname>Nam</surname><given-names>NV</given-names></name><name><surname>Binh</surname><given-names>TQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Chong</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Quoc</surname><given-names>NT</given-names></name><name><surname>Thanh</surname><given-names>TN</given-names></name><name><surname>Hung</surname><given-names>LN</given-names></name><name><surname>Kager</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Control of malaria: a successful experience from Viet Nam</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>2002</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>660</fpage><lpage>666</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12219158</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Erhart</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Thang</surname><given-names>ND</given-names></name><name><surname>Bien</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Tung</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hung</surname><given-names>NQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hung</surname><given-names>LX</given-names></name><name><surname>Tuy</surname><given-names>TQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Speybroeck</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Cong</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name><name><surname>Coosemans</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>D'Alessandro</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Malaria epidemiology in a rural are